<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How the Northwest Arkansas Audubon Society handles your information.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated November 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    The Northwest Arkansas Audubon Society (NWAAS) is a volunteer-run non-profit. We collect as
    little information as we can. This page explains what we do have and how we use it.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not have accounts or sign-in, and it does not ask you to enter personal
    information on its pages. Like most websites, our hosting provider (Netlify) may keep standard
    server logs, such as visitors' IP addresses, to run and secure the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Emails and field trip sign-ups</h2>
  <p>
    When you email us, or RSVP for a field trip, we use the information you send (such as your
    name, email address, and the number of people attending) to reply to you and to organize the
    trip. We keep this in our records to run field trips and to contact participants about them.
    We do not sell or share it, other than with NWAAS volunteers who need it to do their work.
  </p>

  <p>
    Field trip leaders choose to publish their own contact information (such as an email address
    or phone number) on trip pages so participants can reach them.
  </p>

  <h2>Donations and memberships</h2>
  <p>
    Online donations are processed by PayPal, which has its own privacy policy. NWAAS does not
    receive or store your card number. If you mail a check, our treasurer records your name,
    address and gift amount for our financial records and to acknowledge your gift.
  </p>

  <h2>Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to other websites, such as eBird, Facebook and YouTube. They have their own
    privacy practices, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    To ask us about your information, or to ask us to remove it, email
    <a href="mailto:info@nwarkaudubon.org">info@nwarkaudubon.org</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
